MK_T_BG_BLOCK="[@TAG@-SUBAGENT-BG] You are returning while background work you started is still running:
%s
A report written before it finishes is not evidence. Do not return yet.
For a Bash task: wait for it in the FOREGROUND with one Bash call whose timeout parameter is 600000,
looping until its output file shows it finished (the file path was in the tool result that started it).
For a Monitor task (no output file): run its wait condition in the foreground the same way, or stop
it with TaskStop. Then read the result and finish your report. TaskOutput is not available to subagents.
If it is a server or watcher you no longer need, stop it with TaskStop (ToolSearch \"select:TaskStop\").
Next time pass timeout: 600000 on the Bash call so a normal run stays in the foreground; 600000 is a
cap, not a guarantee, so a run can still end up backgrounded -- if that happens, wait for it before
returning, the same way."
MK_T_BG_LAST_BLOCK="This is the last block. If you still cannot wait, stop the task with TaskStop and make the first
line of your final report: [@TAG@-SUBAGENT-BG] UNFINISHED: %s"
MK_T_PC_SUMMARY="Bu özette şunları mutlaka koru: aktif faz ve dilim, sıradaki TEK adım, açık bloklar ve alınan kararlar, son commit'ler, docs/STATE.md'nin güncel olup olmadığı (değilse neyin eksik kaldığı). Ayrıntılı geçmiş anlatısını, tekrar eden araç çıktılarını ve kapanmış ara adımları at — tarihsel kayıt docs/HISTORY.md'de tutuluyor."
